  "exp": "The classic 'iron triangle' of project management is Time, Cost and Scope (with quality often shown at the centre, affected by changes to any of the three): tightening one constraint forces trade-offs in the others. Options B, C and D substitute plausible-sounding project terms (manager/team/customer, resource, profit) that are not the three vertices of the traditional triangle taught in every PM foundations course.",
  "prov": "Official MPSC final answer key",
