  "sub": "Seating arrangement",
  "q": "Five friends A, B, C, D and E sit in a single row of five seats, numbered 1 (leftmost) to 5 (rightmost), one person per seat. C sits at seat 1. B sits immediately to the right of A. D sits exactly between B and E (that is, B, D and E occupy three consecutive seats with D in the middle). What is the correct seating order from seat 1 to seat 5?",
  "opts": {
   "A": "C, A, B, D, E",
   "B": "C, E, D, B, A",
   "C": "C, B, A, D, E",
   "D": "C, A, D, B, E"
  },
  "ans": "A",
  "exp": "C occupies seat 1, leaving seats 2-5 for A, B, D, E. Since B must be immediately right of A, and B, D, E must occupy three consecutive seats with D in the middle, the only way to fit both constraints into the remaining 4 seats is the continuous block A, B, D, E at seats 2, 3, 4, 5: A(2), B(3) satisfies 'B immediately right of A', and B(3), D(4), E(5) satisfies 'D between B and E'. Testing the reverse block E, D, B, A fails, since that would put B to the right of A rather than A immediately left of B. So the order is C, A, B, D, E.",
  "prov": "Authored to cover a syllabus sub-topic with no past-question coverage",
