  "srcKey": "TECH2_2021",
  "no": 19,
  "paper": "TECH2",
  "unit": "4",
  "sub": "Symptoms of Poor Governance",
  "q": "Poor governance may be identified by signs of:",
  "opts": {
   "A": "Multiple visit to government office",
   "B": "Service is a right",
   "C": "Corrupt officers",
   "D": "Personal information exchange"
  },
  "ans": "A",
  "conf": "low",
  "exp": "In the citizen-experience framing used in e-governance material, having to make repeated visits to a government office is the textbook symptom of poor governance and the pain point e-governance is designed to remove. The question is defective because corrupt officers is equally a sign of poor governance; option B (service as a right) describes good governance.",
  "prov": "Derived by a single solver — the bank held no answer for this question and MPSC published no key. Unverified.",
