  "srcKey": "TECH2_2021",
  "no": 27,
  "paper": "TECH2",
  "unit": "2",
  "sub": "Implementation approach and sourcing",
  "q": "The implications of having single vendor is:",
  "opts": {
   "A": "Better suited for large agencies with highly specific and strategic ICT functions",
   "B": "Provides greater control over vendor performance",
   "C": "Requires higher capacities in the department and higher coordination risk",
   "D": "Optimum option if all the components for external sourcing can be bundled into one group"
  },
  "ans": "D",
  "conf": "medium",
  "exp": "Single-vendor (prime vendor) sourcing is the optimum choice when all externally sourced components can be bundled into one package under one point of accountability. Options A and C describe the multi-vendor model, which is what demands higher departmental capacity and carries coordination risk.",
  "prov": "Derived by a single solver — the bank held no answer for this question and MPSC published no key. Unverified.",
