  "sub": "Firewall",
  "q": "Which of the below is false in regards to the usage of firewall?",
  "opts": {
   "A": "Firewall performs application-level screening",
   "B": "Application level firewall capture and compare packets to state information in connection tables",
   "C": "Firewall may provide additional services such as DHCP,NAT",
   "D": "Application level firewalls provide the strongest level of security and is the fastest"
  },
  "ans": "D",
  "conf": "medium",
  "exp": "Application-level (proxy) firewalls do give the strongest security, but because they inspect the full application payload they are the slowest, not the fastest, so the statement is false. Note that option B is loosely worded too - comparing packets against connection-state tables actually describes stateful inspection - but D is the plainly false claim the question is after.",
