  "paper": "TECH2",
  "unit": "13",
  "sub": "Total cost of ownership arguments",
  "q": "Statement 1 : Government choose Open Source System so that it can share development costs with other users\nStatement 2 : Government choose Open Source System so that it can copy repeatedly at no additional cost",
  "opts": {
   "A": "Both statements are false",
   "B": "Statement 1 is true and Statement 2 is false",
   "C": "Both statements are true",
   "D": "Statement 1 is false and Statement 2 is true"
  },
  "ans": "C",
  "conf": "medium",
  "exp": "Both are genuine reasons governments adopt open source: development cost can be shared across a community of users, and once acquired the software can be replicated across departments and offices at no additional licence cost. Neither statement is false as written.",
