  "unit": "13",
  "sub": "Defining Open Source",
  "q": "Which of the following is not a criteria for determining whether or not a software license is open source?",
  "opts": {
   "A": "Free Redistribution",
   "B": "License must be technology dependent",
   "C": "Source code",
   "D": "License should not be specific to a product"
  },
  "ans": "B",
  "conf": "high",
  "exp": "The Open Source Definition explicitly requires a licence to be technology-neutral, so demanding technology dependence is the opposite of a criterion. Free redistribution, availability of source code and the licence not being specific to a product are all listed OSD criteria.",
