  "sub": "ADKAR Model for Change Management",
  "q": "Effective management of people dimension of change requires the following key goals:",
  "opts": {
   "A": "Business Need,Design",
   "B": "Identify Obstacles, Reinforcement",
   "C": "Desire,Ability",
   "D": "Determine Implementation, Re-Engineering"
  },
  "ans": "C",
  "conf": "medium",
  "exp": "The people side of change is normally taught through the ADKAR model - Awareness, Desire, Knowledge, Ability, Reinforcement - and only option C gives two genuine ADKAR elements. Option B mixes one real element (Reinforcement) with 'identify obstacles', which is a project activity rather than a people-dimension goal.",
  "prov": "Derived by a single solver — the bank held no answer for this question and MPSC published no key. Unverified.",
