  "paper": "TECH2",
  "unit": "14",
  "sub": "Communication in change management",
  "q": "Key Principles of Effective Communication.\nPrinciple 1 : Organisational Change cannot occur without communication\nPrinciple 2 : Communication is a single component of change process\nPrinciple 3 : Communication planning applies to stakeholders, message delivery",
  "opts": {
   "A": "Principle 1 is correct, Principle 2 & 3 are wrong",
   "B": "Principle 2 is correct, Principle 1 & 3 are wrong",
   "C": "Principle 3 is correct, Principle 1 & 2 are wrong",
   "D": "Principle 1,2,3 are correct"
  },
  "ans": "D",
  "conf": "medium",
  "exp": "Principles 1 and 3 are both plainly correct, which rules out options A, B and C, so the intended reading of Principle 2 must be the standard caution that communication is only one component of change management and cannot carry the change on its own. Awkward phrasing of Principle 2 makes this one read badly, but D is the only internally consistent choice.",
