  "unit": "14",
  "sub": "Key reasons for failures in change initiatives",
  "q": "Key reason for failure in change initiative may be:",
  "opts": {
   "A": "There is continuity in the project team",
   "B": "The requirement of the customer is taken into account",
   "C": "Every activity is given equal importance and priority",
   "D": "Benefits at individual level are demonstrated"
  },
  "ans": "C",
  "conf": "medium",
  "exp": "Treating every activity as equally important means nothing is prioritised, effort is spread thin and the critical changes never get the attention they need - a well-known cause of change-programme failure. The other three options describe healthy conditions (team continuity, customer requirements captured, individual benefits shown) that support success rather than cause failure.",
